# Rust
target/
src-tauri/target/

# Node (build-time only -- see overview.md §1)
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local
# The Phase 7 measurement harness's bundle. Built on demand by `npm run profile`; it must
# never ship, which is why it is a separate Vite mode and a separate directory.
dist-profile/
# Scratch: the compiled WKWebView runner, the pages the probes serve, downloaded models, and
# any profile JSON. Nothing in here is tracked and nothing in here is an input to a build.
/build/

# Tauri generated
src-tauri/gen/

# Models are release assets, never repo artifacts (Phase 3)
*.onnx
*.onnx.partial
# ...except the ~130 KB synthetic graphs that let `tests/session.rs` exercise `ort` against
# a real ONNX Runtime without a 200 MB download. Generated by
# `scripts/make_session_fixtures.py`; they compute nonsense on purpose. See that script.
!src-tauri/tests/fixtures/session/*.onnx

# Build products
*.dmg
*.app/

# Local app data, if it is ever symlinked into the tree for debugging
/appdata
/Application Support

# Data layer artifacts (Phase 1). The real ones live in
# ~/Library/Application Support/<bundle-id>/; these patterns exist so a copy pulled into
# the tree for debugging cannot be committed by accident. Every byte of them is derived
# from the user's own files.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
embeddings.bin
embeddings.bin.compacting

# The one-time ONNX export environment (scripts/export_clap_onnx.py). Developer-only and
# never part of a build -- see overview.md 1 on why Python does not ship.
.venv*/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
